    "diagnosis": "Benign notochordal cell tumour",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<strong>A</strong> Sagittal T1-weighted MRI. Focal midline hypointense delineated lesion in the L5 vertebral body. Small hyperintense punctiform intralesional foci are seen (arrows), which correspond to entrapped fatty bone marrow. <strong>B</strong> Axial T1-weighted MRI. Focal hypointense bone lesion with clear margins and preservation of the trabecular architecture including in the periphery (arrowheads). <strong>C</strong> Sagittal T2-weighted MRI with fat suppression. Hyperintense signal intensity of the lesion without perilesional oedema or extraosseous extension (arrowhead). <strong>D</strong> Axial CT of L5 demonstrates osteosclerosis throughout the midline tumorous lesion and no osteolytic changes in the vertebral body. Small intralesional fat components are seen on CT due to entrapped fat (arrows).",
    "source": "Ana Navas Cañete",
